package Libraries.Game.Graphics.Shaders.Vulkan.Mapping

use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Shaders.Vulkan.VulkanShaderProgram
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Vulkan.VulkanDevice
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Vulkan.VulkanPipelineInfo
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Vulkan.VulkanPipelineInfoCreator

/*
TransparentShaderMapping3DVulkan describes the pipeline for see-through
models: a forward program, drawn after
the deferred lighting, over the lit image, with the default 3D vertex data,
the G-buffer, the lights, the sky and the sky light (sets 0 to 5, see
VulkanPipelineInfoCreator:AddForwardInfo3D). It blends by alpha, with no
depth test and no culling; the fragment shader hides back faces of one-sided
materials. The program's own 18 push constant numbers are unused (zeros).

Attribute: Example
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Shaders.Vulkan.Mapping.TransparentShaderMapping3DVulkan

TransparentShaderMapping3DVulkan mapping
*/
class TransparentShaderMapping3DVulkan is VulkanShaderMapping
    on create
        UseDefaultResources3D(true)
        UseForwardPass(true)
    end

    /*
    This action makes the pipeline description for see-through models.

    Attribute: Parameter program The program.
    Attribute: Parameter device The Vulkan device.
    Attribute: Returns The pipeline description.
    */
    action CreatePipelineInfo(VulkanShaderProgram program, VulkanDevice device) returns VulkanPipelineInfo
        VulkanPipelineInfoCreator creator
        creator:Begin(device)
        creator:AddForwardInfo3D()
        return creator:Finish()
    end
end
